- Use transactions for critical operations.
- Prevent duplicate reservations.
- Prevent overbooking.
- Avoid competing sources of truth.
- Use database constraints where appropriate.

## 7.3 Security

- Enforce RLS.
- Validate all untrusted input.
- Protect privileged operations.
- Use server-side secrets.
- Apply least-privilege access.
- Prevent unauthorized access to private documents.
- Protect webhook endpoints.
- Avoid exposing unnecessary personal information.

## 7.4 Maintainability

- Reuse existing components.
- Follow existing naming conventions.
- Keep modules focused.
- Avoid unnecessary abstraction.
- Avoid duplicate business logic.
- Document important architectural decisions.
- Include appropriate error handling and logging.

## 7.5 Performance

- Avoid unnecessary database requests.
- Avoid loading entire datasets into the frontend.
- Use pagination where appropriate.
- Use efficient SQL aggregation.
- Avoid unnecessary dependencies.
- Consider caching carefully.
- Avoid repeated external API requests.

